# novadeck: enable the first-boot Steam seeder on release. It stages the baked Steam seed into the
# writable /home/deck and is ordered Before=sddm.service, so the shell has its client before SDDM
# autologins deck. /etc/machine-id is empty on a fresh image so systemd runs preset-all on first boot
# (stock 99-default.preset is "disable *"); this higher-priority preset (60 < 99) keeps it enabled. A
# build-time graphical.target.wants symlink ships alongside as a fallback. The seeder self-skips the
# ~1GB copy once staged, so steady-state boots pay only the cheap ownership-repair.
enable novadeck-steam-bootstrap.service
